<<<
incarnate. Pronounce the verb V/nkarnat, & the adjective inkar‘nit. For adj. in -able, see -ATABLE.
===
**incarnate.** Pronounce the verb ĭ'nkarnāt, & the adjective ĭnkar'nĭt. For adj. in *-able*, see ^^-ATABLE^^.
>>>

<<<
incarnation. This unfortunately is not the prisoner’s first lapse from honesty, for when the Chief Consiable of Peterborough said ‘he was the very quintessence of cunning & the incarnation of a book-thief’, he was not speaking without knowledge.
===
**incarnation.** *This unfortunately is not the prisoner's first lapse from honesty, for when the Chief Constable of Peterborough said ' he was the very quintessence of cunning & the incarnation of a book-thief ', he was not speaking without knowledge.*
>>>
